{
  "record_id": "batch.motif.african-nursery-tales-zulus-callaway-archive-l38333-l38424",
  "source_text_path": "texts/public-domain/zulu/project-gutenberg/nursery-tales-traditions-histories-zulus-callaway.md",
  "passage_locator": {
    "label": "KEY  TO  THE  RIDDLES. / IZIKGANEKWANE. / KEY  TO  THE  RIDDLES. / IZINGANEKWANE.; lines 38333-38424",
    "start": "38333",
    "end": "38424",
    "translation": "Nursery Tales, Traditions, and Histories of the Zulus, in Their Own Words",
    "notes": "Stable markdown line range generated from canonical text."
  },
  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "There, then, is the man who is in the midst of enemies, the tongue.",
    "summary": "This key to several riddles explains that the tongue, moving between teeth as they chew and \"kill\" food, is like a man living among enemies in a place of battle. It then describes the closing-poles of a cattle-pen which, by closing the gateway at night, watch and confine the cattle until morning, when the gateway is opened and the poles lie on the ground. Finally, it notes that the ten fingers are matched and go in pairs, with a comment identifying particular paired fingers.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The tongue is said to be not happy when the teeth are chewing food.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "When the teeth chew food, the tongue continually moves from side to side between the teeth.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The food is described as being constantly \"killed\" by the teeth during chewing.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The tongue is not killed by the teeth because it is known and is called a man of that place.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The tongue dwells in a place where there is fighting and continually meets with accidents.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The tongue is happy before food is eaten but, when food is being eaten, it knows it is in the midst of danger.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The tongue expects to be injured or to die because a battle is fought in its presence, despite no charge having been made against it.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The explanation concludes that the man who is in the midst of enemies is the tongue.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The closing-poles of the cattle-pen watch the cattle at night by closing the gateway.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The closing-poles are set close together so that the cattle may not find a place of escape.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Even if a beast tries to get out, it cannot do so because of the strength of the bars.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "By morning the cattle have not got out; then the gateway is opened, the cattle go out, and the closing-poles lie on the ground.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The fingers are said to be ten in number and to be matched, going in pairs.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "The explanation refers to particular pairs of fingers, with a note that the original means the index and middle fingers and the thumbs.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3",
        "ev:4"
      ]
    }
  ],
