      "locator": "lines 485-497",
      "quote_or_summary": "The author notes that old manuscripts have words run together and that cuneiform inscriptions first appeared as a conglomerate of wedges, raising doubts about whether they were writing or ornament. He reports that a sign was discovered in these inscriptions to separate words, which Max Muller calls an immense help for decipherment.",
