      "text": "The boy goes rapidly and, when he hears the people are near, repeats the phrase “Ubongopa-kamagadhlela” and tells them to stand still, asking if they do not see they are being killed by thieves of another tribe.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "After the boy speaks, the cattle stand still.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The people shout to the boy to stand still in that place so that they may kill him, saying that he has long practised magic.",
